 70| /// What a strictness level means in gate terms.
 71| ///
 72| /// The defaults are deliberately quiet. A reviewer that raises four things on
 73| /// every pull request gets read for a week and ignored thereafter, and the
 74| /// findings people actually want — a real bug, a leaked credential — are the
 75| /// ones that get lost in that noise. Level 2 posts high-severity findings the
 76| /// model is genuinely confident about, and folds everything else into the
 77| /// summary where it costs nobody anything to skim.
 78| #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
